    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4807" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bacchylĭdēs</span></b> ,
			is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βακχυλίδης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Greek lyric poet of Ceos</i>, <i>a
				nephew of Simonides</i>, who lived about 470 B.C.,
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 25, 4,
			3</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bacchylĭdĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of
			Bacchylides</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Centim. 2, 5, p. 1819</span></i>
			 P.</div>
